            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0187" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg175"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.24/538: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-01T21:00:00-05:00">June 1, 1943—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 2—3:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>946. United Press reports appearing in Colombian press May 31 quotes Hector Lazo
                    of the Board of Economic Warfare<anchor n="12" xml:id="d171-f1"/> as stating
                    that the Decentralization Plan will be applied in the future only on articles
                    subject to control by War Production Board. Please telegraph urgently whether
                    this statement is true as the effect on the local certifying agency of this
                    unconfirmed report is further to delay the issuance of Import
                    Recommendations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d171-f1" n="12" xml:id="d171-f1-content">
                <p>Assistant Director in charge of the Office of Exports.</p>
